{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Acceptance-criteria evidence gathered read-only against merged state `c4c070287818103c1c39d55b9e21d1b76cd81994` in `/Users/joeoakhart/rebar/.rebar/worktrees/verify-0eba-runs` and `/Users/joeoakhart/rebar/.rebar/worktrees/verify-0eba`.\n\n| # | Verdict | Evidence |\n|---:|---|---|\n| 1 | MET | Completed sandbox run: `/Users/joeoakhart/rebar/.rebar/worktrees/verify-0eba-runs/.rebar/scratch/verify-0eba-runs-45483/make-test.log` records `33 failed, 20149 passed, 126 skipped, 21 warnings in 1912.43s`, `MAKE_TEST_EXIT=2`, and `MAKE_TEST_SEMLOCK_COUNT=0`. The same log reports counted compatibility skips, not SemLock failures: `POSIX named semaphore unavailable: [Errno 1] Operation not permitted: 4`. |\n| 2 | MET | Fresh exact command run from the merged worktree: `env PATH=\"/Users/joeoakhart/rebar/.rebar/worktrees/fix-2d65-autodeploy/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make verify`; log `/Users/joeoakhart/rebar/.rebar/worktrees/verify-0eba-runs/.rebar/scratch/evidence-0eba-11991/make-verify-exact.log` records `HEAD=c4c070287818103c1c39d55b9e21d1b76cd81994`, reaches the pytest summary, and exits normally with `MAKE_VERIFY_EXIT=2` after `33 failed, 20149 passed, 126 skipped`. This is a verdict-producing failure, not the prior semaphore abort. |\n| 3 | MET | `tests/test_sandbox_capabilities_0eba.py:13-22` defines `test_posix_named_semaphore_probe_reports_unavailable_on_eperm`, raising `PermissionError(errno.EPERM, \"Operation not permitted\")` and asserting `not probe.available` plus `POSIX named semaphore unavailable` in the reason. Targeted run artifact `/Users/joeoakhart/rebar/.rebar/worktrees/verify-0eba/.rebar/scratch/verify-0eba-84728/targeted-sandbox-tests.log` records `pytest -q tests/test_sandbox_capabilities_0eba.py`, `4 passed in 1.07s`, `EXIT_CODE=0`. |\n| 4 | MET | `tests/test_sandbox_capabilities_0eba.py:26-40` asserts the success path reports available. Scratch mutation evidence `/Users/joeoakhart/rebar/.rebar/worktrees/verify-0eba/.rebar/scratch/verify-0eba-84728/available-test-with-constant-unavailable.log` records the constant-unavailable stub causing `AssertionError: assert False` at line 37 and `EXIT_CODE=1`; `/Users/joeoakhart/rebar/.rebar/worktrees/verify-0eba/.rebar/scratch/verify-0eba-84728/available-test-restored.log` records the restored test as `1 passed`, `EXIT_CODE=0`, with no remaining diff shown. |\n| 5 | PARTIAL | CI job evidence exists for the merged patchset run: `/Users/joeoakhart/rebar/.rebar/worktrees/verify-0eba/.rebar/scratch/verify-0eba-84728/gh-run-35383290639-jobs.json` shows `build-and-test (gate + suite on the patchset) / pytest (ubuntu-latest, py3.13)` completed `success`, and `/Users/joeoakhart/rebar/.rebar/worktrees/verify-0eba/.rebar/scratch/verify-0eba-84728/ci-ubuntu-py313-filtered.log` reports `20347 passed, 82 skipped`. The same log names 2 of the 4 affected tests in warnings (`test_two_processes_publish_at_most_one_equivalent_same_ticket_bundle`, `test_a_contended_fcntl_leg_reads_as_held`), but quiet pytest output does not name the other 2 passing tests or provide per-test skip lists. Static marker evidence shows exactly the 4 tests are marked (`tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_atomic_completion_close.py:395`, `tests/scripts/graph/test_doctor_locks.py:150`, `tests/unit/test_marker_fcntl_guard.py:80`, `tests/unit/test_network_guard_local_ipc.py:71`), and docs state hosted runners provide POSIX named semaphores, but the saved CI artifact does not directly prove all 4 executed rather than skipped. Missing: collected/per-test CI output or JUnit results showing all 4 had non-skipped outcomes. |\n| 6 | MET | `tests/test_sandbox_capabilities_0eba.py:44-98` asserts the absent-capability path reports all 4 skips with `result.assert